  "notes": "USAGE:\nA godan verb ({漉|こ}す → {漉|こ}します). Often written in hiragana as こす since the kanji {漉|こ} is not in the standard-use kanji list. Primarily a cooking and craft term.\n\nNote: The homophones {越|こ}す (to cross over) and {超|こ}す (to exceed) are completely different words.\n\nAlso used in the compound {紙|かみ}を{漉|す}く (to make paper by hand), though this uses a different reading of the same kanji.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {布|ぬの}で{漉|こ}す: to strain through cloth\n- ざるで{漉|こ}す: to strain through a colander\n- {裏|うら}{漉|ご}し: straining through a sieve (noun form)\n- だしを{漉|こ}す: to strain stock",
